+# Pagemark Privacy Policy
+
+Last updated: 2026-10-12
+
+Pagemark is a private, fully local book tracker. It has no accounts, no server, no analytics, no advertising and no telemetry. The developer (AxialForge) receives no data from the app.
+
+## What is stored
+Your books, reads, ratings, notes, shelves, tags and settings are stored only in a database on your device. Your optional PIN is stored as a salted PBKDF2 hash in the device's secure storage. The app's event log (errors only, never book titles or thoughts) stays on the device.
+
+## What leaves your device
+- **Book lookup:** when you search by title or ISBN, the search text or ISBN is sent to Open Library (openlibrary.org) to fetch book details and covers. No account or identifier is attached by Pagemark. Open Library's own privacy policy applies.
+- **Google Drive backup (optional, off by default):** if you set it up and sign in, an encrypted-or-plain copy of your database is uploaded to the hidden app-data folder of *your own* Google Drive. Pagemark never sees your Google credentials, and the developer cannot access the backup.
+- **Camera:** used only to scan ISBN barcodes on the device. Images are not stored or transmitted.
+
+## Exports
+CSV/JSON exports and database exports are saved or shared only where you choose. Locked-library books are excluded from CSV/JSON exports; the full database export and Drive backup include them.
+
+## Deleting your data
+Uninstalling Pagemark deletes its local data. Drive backups can be deleted from Google Drive settings (Manage apps).
+
+## Children
+Pagemark is not directed at children under 13 and collects no personal information.
+
+## Contact
+Open an issue at https://github.com/AxialForge/Pagemark/issues or email josephkresevic@gmail.com.
